%description:

Tcp.tcpEcnMode:rfc3168 -- the SYN of host1 has ECE and CWR; its SYN-ACK to an AccECN SYN has ECE: ECN.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "ECN: "off": no ECN; "passive": answer an ECN-setup SYN (RFC 3168), but
request no ECN in an active open ...; "rfc3168": request and answer ECN; "accecn": request
Accurate ECN (RFC 9768), and answer it and ECN; "accecn-passive": answer Accurate ECN and ECN,
but request nothing. Each connection reads it at its open".

The classes: off (the value of LegacyTcp), passive (the default), rfc3168, accecn,
accecn-passive, and changed (the value changes during the run; the parameter is @mutable).
The code: TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() reads the mode at the open; the SYN of an
active open requests ECN (ECE, CWR) with "rfc3168" and AccECN (AE, CWR, ECE) with "accecn";
a passive connection answers an AccECN SYN with AccECN ("accecn", "accecn-passive"), with
ECN (ECE; "passive", "rfc3168"), or not at all ("off"). This test separates "rfc3168" from the other values.

Host under test: host1, which opens a connection to host2 at 0.1 s, and listens on port 2000;
host2 requests AccECN (tcpEcnMode "accecn", a precondition) and opens a connection to host1 at
0.3 s. Each value gives another pair: the ECN bits of the SYN of host1, and those of its
SYN-ACK. An AccECN SYN-ACK feeds back the IP ECN field of the SYN, here Not-ECT: AE 0, CWR 1,
ECE 0 (RFC 9768 Table 2). Observation: level 1, the SYN of host1 has ECE and CWR, and its SYN-ACK has ECE: ECN.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpEcnMode
%# class: rfc3168
%# value: "rfc3168"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpTcpEcnModeRfc3168")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.aeBit == false && tcp.cwrBit == true && tcp.eceBit == true")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.aeBit == false && tcp.cwrBit == false && tcp.eceBit == true")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of host1 to the AccECN SYN of host2")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpTcpEcnModeRfc3168 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "rfc3168"    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.host1.numApps = 2
*.host1.app[1].typename = "TcpEchoApp"
*.host1.app[1].localPort = 2000
*.host1.app[1].echoFactor = 0
*.host2.numApps = 2
*.host2.app[1].typename = "TcpSessionApp"
*.host2.app[1].connectAddress = "host1"
*.host2.app[1].connectPort = 2000
*.host2.app[1].tOpen = 0.3s
*.host2.app[1].tSend = 0.4s
*.host2.app[1].sendBytes = 1000B
*.host2.app[1].tClose = 1000s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpTcpEcnModeRfc3168: PASS
